WEBVTT

01:30.310 --> 01:35.190
<b><u>Episode 12
</u>When I Cough, 
It's the Two of Us</b>

01:30.680 --> 01:32.730
Wow, it's Shy!

01:32.730 --> 01:34.040
You're Japan's hero, aren't you?

01:32.730 --> 01:35.530
Um, uh...

01:34.040 --> 01:35.530
What are you doing in Russia?

01:35.530 --> 01:37.490
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

01:37.490 --> 01:38.840
Shy!

01:40.780 --> 01:43.490
Hang on, please!

01:44.840 --> 01:45.780
Pesha.

01:46.950 --> 01:49.480
It looks like everyone 
inside is all right, too.

01:49.480 --> 01:51.750
Dr. Isaak is checking on them now.

01:52.180 --> 01:54.490
Oh, that's great.

01:54.490 --> 01:56.420
But you know...

01:56.650 --> 01:59.300
I guess you really are a hero.

02:00.630 --> 02:03.920
Having someone tell me that to my 
face is actually sorta embarrassing.

02:03.920 --> 02:05.310
Oh, please!

02:06.050 --> 02:08.460
But I knew it...

02:08.460 --> 02:09.450
Knew what?

02:10.080 --> 02:14.370
I knew you'd make something 
of yourself someday.

02:14.370 --> 02:17.070
M-Me? Why would you think that?

02:17.320 --> 02:24.080
Well... Because Lenya loved you very much.

02:25.200 --> 02:26.500
Mama?

02:26.500 --> 02:29.480
Oh, don't get the wrong idea, though.

02:29.480 --> 02:32.590
It's not all thanks to her.

02:33.080 --> 02:37.090
Lenya was someone I really looked up to.

02:37.420 --> 02:39.980
What? This is the first time I'm hearing that.

02:39.980 --> 02:42.770
Well, of course it is. It's the 
first time I've ever said it.

02:43.680 --> 02:48.630
Lenya never acted like a child, 
even when she was one.

02:49.930 --> 02:57.070
Even when something bad happened, 
I never saw her cry or throw a fit.

02:57.890 --> 03:02.380
I think that's just how her parents raised her.

03:03.240 --> 03:08.700
Like, "Don't cause trouble for others. 
Don't rely on others, either."

03:09.650 --> 03:14.760
But to put it another way, 
she did so much for others.

03:15.250 --> 03:17.970
She was very devoted and never 
expected anything in return.

03:17.970 --> 03:21.260
I'm pretty sure that didn't 
change once she became an adult.

03:22.110 --> 03:25.300
There were some who mocked Lenya and 
called her stupid because of that.

03:25.300 --> 03:27.910
She went through so many hardships.

03:28.640 --> 03:30.270
But even so, I...

03:32.020 --> 03:38.090
I admired the fact that she was like a 
hero who dedicated her life to others.

03:40.080 --> 03:43.920
That's why, even now that you're a real hero,

03:43.920 --> 03:47.910
you still carry her blood and 
the love she gave to you.

03:48.440 --> 03:52.810
When I really thought about it, 
it just made perfect sense.

03:53.680 --> 03:57.580
In my eyes, you and your 
mother are both heroes.

03:57.580 --> 03:59.300
Two generations' worth.

04:00.010 --> 04:01.350
Natalia-san...

04:05.600 --> 04:07.000
P-Pepesha-san!

04:07.000 --> 04:07.900
Oh, dear.

04:07.900 --> 04:10.930
S-Save me! Help!

04:11.190 --> 04:14.130
Oh, my. Looks like our hero's in trouble.

04:14.130 --> 04:17.940
Kids, wrap it up and head inside!

04:17.940 --> 04:19.320
Okay!

04:22.480 --> 04:24.620
Y-You saved mwee...

04:25.620 --> 04:27.380
<i>Teru? Teru!</i>

04:27.970 --> 04:28.700
Shrimpy-san?

04:29.550 --> 04:31.940
<i>Thank goodness you're safe.</i>

04:31.940 --> 04:34.710
<i>I couldn't get a hold of you 
for a while, so I was worried.</i>

04:34.710 --> 04:36.640
I-I'm fine.

04:36.640 --> 04:41.960
I've... well... Pepesha-san and I were 
able to take care of the situation.

04:42.480 --> 04:46.560
<i>I see. Unilord just sent 
reinforcements your way.</i>

04:46.560 --> 04:47.130
Huh?

04:50.220 --> 04:52.220
I heard there was an emergency...

04:53.070 --> 04:54.940
But it looks like it's been taken care of.

04:54.940 --> 04:58.480
Stardust! Lady Black! You came to help us?

04:58.480 --> 05:02.490
Yeah. Just before you got here,

05:02.910 --> 05:05.550
we received a transmission from Unilord.

05:06.920 --> 05:10.240
Just now, the governments 
and heroes of all nations

05:10.640 --> 05:14.630
have agreed to share information 
and cooperate with each other.

05:15.410 --> 05:18.330
Which means that the next 
time Amarariruku appears,

05:18.680 --> 05:22.090
the nations of the world will work 
together to solve the problem.

05:22.500 --> 05:27.680
While that was going on, we received 
word that you were being attacked...

05:28.200 --> 05:29.600
But I guess we weren't needed.

05:29.860 --> 05:34.100
I'll personally fill Unilord 
in on the details later.

05:34.500 --> 05:38.600
I can't leave this place until 
I know that everyone's safe.

05:38.860 --> 05:42.610
I see. Is there anything else I can help with?

05:42.940 --> 05:44.360
There is one thing.

05:45.120 --> 05:45.900
Here.

05:46.770 --> 05:50.620
This ring... It's one that 
Amarariruku left behind.

05:50.940 --> 05:53.860
Could you deliver this 
to Unilord immediately?

05:54.540 --> 05:57.120
I see. Got it.

05:57.670 --> 05:59.870
Well, I'm gonna head back.

05:59.870 --> 06:01.670
I'm a busy man, you know.

06:02.530 --> 06:03.860
U-Um!

06:05.610 --> 06:09.570
Th-Thank you for your guidance the other day!

06:09.570 --> 06:13.010
Because of that, I was able 
to save a lot of people today.

06:13.900 --> 06:17.120
I've been meaning to tell you that for 
a while, but kept missing my chance...

06:17.120 --> 06:19.770
So... I'm sorry.

06:24.540 --> 06:28.380
Oh, it's you. The one I met on the spaceship.

06:29.620 --> 06:32.150
Right, that did happen, didn't it?

06:32.150 --> 06:34.280
<i>He totally forgot about me...</i>

06:34.960 --> 06:38.430
I didn't do anything you need to thank me for.

06:38.430 --> 06:41.060
You just got stronger on your own.

06:42.290 --> 06:46.670
Once you accomplish something, 
it's not because of someone else.

06:47.510 --> 06:52.180
Just like when you're unable to do 
anything, it's not anyone else's fault.

06:53.190 --> 06:54.830
So be proud of yourself.

06:55.540 --> 06:59.080
When you're able to think that 
you've truly saved someone,

06:59.080 --> 07:02.190
that pride will change into your next power.

07:03.580 --> 07:06.200
If a hero's back is always doubled over,

07:06.200 --> 07:09.190
it'll make the person they saved 
want to apologize, too.

07:09.560 --> 07:12.200
Like, "I'm sorry for making you save me."

07:13.330 --> 07:15.180
Well, I'm heading back now.

07:16.130 --> 07:19.200
I'll leave the rest to you, Lady Black.

07:19.680 --> 07:20.870
Got it.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.060
I'll check to see if anyone's injured.

07:28.640 --> 07:31.630
Okay, Shy. Have you checked 
to see if anyone's wounded?

07:31.630 --> 07:33.340
Oh, um...

07:33.340 --> 07:38.650
There are some who were hit by the 
enemy's attack, so I'll lead you to them.

07:38.650 --> 07:39.850
What about you?

07:39.850 --> 07:41.350
Me?

07:42.230 --> 07:45.980
I'm fine! So please, take 
a look at everyone else.

07:46.770 --> 07:47.860
I see.

07:48.160 --> 07:50.450
I like that look on your face now.

07:50.450 --> 07:52.530
Looks like you were able 
to conquer a mountain.

07:57.190 --> 07:58.960
You're leaving already?

07:58.960 --> 08:01.210
You could at least spend a night here.

08:01.630 --> 08:04.720
We can't stay too long and be a burden.

08:04.720 --> 08:06.290
I'll come visit again.

08:06.290 --> 08:09.950
I see. Well, do your best!

08:09.950 --> 08:12.250
Shy, Spirit.

08:12.250 --> 08:14.340
Thanks for saving us.

08:16.470 --> 08:20.180
We're all looking out for you, Pesha.

08:20.920 --> 08:24.000
Thanks, Natalia-san.

08:29.130 --> 08:30.730
Amarariruku...

08:31.120 --> 08:34.740
I wonder what Stigma's really after.

08:35.160 --> 08:39.580
I feel like there's something 
very important there.

08:40.170 --> 08:45.750
Even if we don't know what that is, 
heroes like us need to be fully prepared.

08:45.750 --> 08:48.490
Okay, let's get going!

08:48.490 --> 08:50.200
Uh, s-sure!

08:50.200 --> 08:51.760
But before that...

08:52.180 --> 08:55.130
A bar that I go to all the time is nearby.

08:55.130 --> 08:58.830
Huh?! But you were just drinking 
a whole bunch with Natalia-san.

08:58.830 --> 09:01.640
I'm actually surprised you're still standing...

09:01.640 --> 09:05.420
That was basically an apéritif!

09:05.420 --> 09:09.290
All right! I'm gonna drink! 
I'm gonna drink to my heart's content!

09:09.290 --> 09:11.250
Until I can't drink anymore!

09:11.250 --> 09:12.660
<i>Amarariruku...</i>

09:13.230 --> 09:14.800
<i>The world inside people's hearts...</i>

09:14.800 --> 09:19.410
<i>Stigma's dream that he wants to see come true, 
even if it means warping the dreams of others...</i>

09:21.410 --> 09:26.420
<i>I don't know what it is, but I'm a hero,</i>

09:26.800 --> 09:29.540
<i>and I was asked to stop them.</i>

09:31.120 --> 09:37.050
<i>And that probably doesn't mean
just beating them in a fight...</i>

09:37.510 --> 09:39.960
Teru-chan! I'm gonna leave you behind!

09:39.960 --> 09:42.260
Oh... I-I'll be right there!

09:44.260 --> 09:46.680
Are you gonna say I'm 
drinking too much again?

09:46.680 --> 09:48.560
Well, you do.

09:48.560 --> 09:49.200
Huh?

09:52.440 --> 09:57.030
Even if one's body disappears, 
their heart remains in this world.

09:58.240 --> 10:00.100
Hearts are eternal

10:00.820 --> 10:02.700
and endlessly free.

10:03.960 --> 10:06.660
That's why you don't need 
to be sad, Kufufu-san.

10:07.530 --> 10:12.670
You, Tzveta-chan, me, everyone...

10:14.860 --> 10:18.460
In the end, we'll all become one.

10:23.680 --> 10:24.750
Shy.

10:26.640 --> 10:29.980
<u>Unilord
Nickname: Yunicchi 
Nationality: ??? 
 Likes: Cooking, cleaning, soup 
The one in charge of all the heroes. 
No one has actually seen her face.</u>

10:31.440 --> 10:32.980
Good morning, Momijiyama-san!

10:35.120 --> 10:36.740
Koishikawa-san...

10:37.450 --> 10:38.700
Good morning.

10:41.990 --> 10:45.080
You know that matryoshka doll 
you brought back for me?

10:45.080 --> 10:47.540
My little brother loves it!

10:47.540 --> 10:51.380
We were just talking about the best 
way to display it this morning.

10:52.460 --> 10:53.910
I see...

10:54.730 --> 10:58.370
Um... You seem a bit down.

10:58.370 --> 11:02.760
You just got back to Japan.
I guess you're still exhausted.

11:02.760 --> 11:07.680
Well... a lot did happen, but I'll be fine.

11:07.680 --> 11:10.270
I am a hero, after all.

11:10.600 --> 11:13.610
Are you sure you're okay, Momijiyama-sa—

11:13.610 --> 11:15.070
<b><i>Slam</i></b>

11:15.840 --> 11:18.090
M-Momijiyama-san?!

11:21.570 --> 11:23.780
Yes. She seems to have a cold.

11:24.860 --> 11:28.200
She'll be fine! I'm going to stay by her side.

11:29.560 --> 11:31.330
Right. Goodbye.

11:34.080 --> 11:37.610
Momijiyama-san, I called the school.

11:37.610 --> 11:40.060
Now, let's make sure you 
get plenty of rest today!

11:40.060 --> 11:42.090
I'll stay with you for a little while, at least.

11:42.090 --> 11:45.140
What? But I feel bad...

11:45.140 --> 11:48.190
You can go to school... 
and don't worry about me...

11:49.140 --> 11:52.990
What are you talking about? 
You can barely stay upright.

11:52.990 --> 11:55.340
I'll at least walk you back home.

11:55.340 --> 11:56.980
But...

11:58.720 --> 12:02.480
U-Um, Koishikawa-san, what exactly is going on?

12:02.480 --> 12:04.280
Isn't this easier for you?

12:04.750 --> 12:08.890
Koishikawa Taxi is taking off! JK!

12:08.890 --> 12:11.160
Er, which way was your house again?

12:11.160 --> 12:12.760
Th-That way...

12:12.760 --> 12:13.790
Go!

12:14.200 --> 12:17.350
<i>I-I can't believe I'm getting 
a piggyback ride at my age...</i>

12:17.350 --> 12:19.800
<i>And by someone my age, no less...</i>

12:19.800 --> 12:21.800
<i>I-I'm gonna die.</i>

12:23.040 --> 12:26.390
Anyway, I guess even you catch colds, huh?

12:26.630 --> 12:29.710
Huh? W-Well, of course. I am human.

12:29.710 --> 12:33.480
I just felt like maybe 
heroes wouldn't get sick.

12:33.860 --> 12:36.550
Isn't that weird? It's such a normal thing.

12:39.120 --> 12:43.950
<i>A normal hero wouldn't let anyone 
see them looking this lame...</i>

12:43.950 --> 12:45.580
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

12:47.470 --> 12:49.710
<i>But I wonder why...</i>

12:50.540 --> 12:52.470
<i>I feel so at ease right now.</i>

12:58.850 --> 13:01.290
We made it to your house, Momijiyama-san!

13:01.290 --> 13:03.510
Th-Thank you very much.

13:04.530 --> 13:06.970
Whoa! A-Are you okay?!

13:07.410 --> 13:09.040
I'm sorry...

13:12.260 --> 13:16.540
Momijiyama-san, is there anyone 
here who can watch over you?

13:16.540 --> 13:21.000
Uh, no... Right now, it'd be just Shrimpy-san.

13:21.000 --> 13:22.410
I see...

13:23.310 --> 13:26.290
In that case, I'll go buy 
you some stuff nearby.

13:26.290 --> 13:28.380
Go ahead and get changed and lie down.

13:28.380 --> 13:30.970
Oh, no! That's okay!

13:30.970 --> 13:33.150
You don't need to do all that...

13:33.550 --> 13:36.170
I swear... You always do that!

13:36.170 --> 13:38.250
You try to handle too much on your own!

13:38.610 --> 13:40.550
It's fine, really. Just get some rest.

13:40.550 --> 13:42.500
O-Okay...

13:46.630 --> 13:51.050
<i>I have been fighting quite a bit lately...</i>

13:51.740 --> 13:54.940
<i>Maybe my body and heart 
just couldn't keep up.</i>

13:55.600 --> 14:01.320
<i>Come to think of it, my body did get pretty 
cold during that fight... But, I mean...</i>

14:02.180 --> 14:04.610
<i>How long has it been since I caught a cold?</i>

14:07.260 --> 14:08.500
Are you all right?

14:08.500 --> 14:10.440
Let me know if there's 
anything I can do for you.

14:10.880 --> 14:14.120
Could you... hang up my uniform?

14:14.700 --> 14:15.540
Got it.

14:18.010 --> 14:18.830
There.

14:20.020 --> 14:24.350
<i>Why do I feel so lonely whenever I get sick?</i>

14:24.860 --> 14:28.840
<i>I can't hear anything, and my body's all numb.</i>

14:30.400 --> 14:32.310
<i>Isn't there anyone around?</i>

14:32.950 --> 14:35.630
<i>I just want someone to talk to me...</i>

14:39.840 --> 14:41.120
Are you okay?

14:47.370 --> 14:49.400
Do you think you can eat yet?

14:54.560 --> 14:56.290
Maybe a little...

14:56.790 --> 14:59.250
I made you some rice porridge.
Try eating that.

14:59.640 --> 15:03.500
Once you eat and get some nutrients 
in you, you'll feel better in no time.

15:05.850 --> 15:07.320
Do you not want to eat yet?

15:07.800 --> 15:09.270
Uh, u-um...

15:09.270 --> 15:14.800
It's... really hard to move my hands...

15:14.800 --> 15:17.850
Oh, for goodness' sake, Teru.

15:17.850 --> 15:19.480
You're such a baby.

15:22.010 --> 15:26.400
Come on, you need to eat. 
I'll even blow on it to cool it down.

15:29.920 --> 15:34.570
Hey, could you do that other 
thing you always do for me, too?

15:34.570 --> 15:36.120
What other thing?

15:36.650 --> 15:38.980
When you rub my back...

15:40.010 --> 15:42.800
Could you do that for me, Onee-chan?

15:46.460 --> 15:48.070
I-I-I-I'm so sorry!

15:48.070 --> 15:50.500
I-I was totally talking in my sleep!

15:50.500 --> 15:54.320
Um, please don't get the wrong idea! 
Just forget what I said! Forget all of it!

15:54.320 --> 15:55.910
Momijiyama-san...

15:56.870 --> 15:58.850
Do you want me to rub your back?

15:58.850 --> 16:00.480
Huh?!

16:00.480 --> 16:03.980
Sure! I'll totally do that for you! 
Here, give me your back!

16:00.960 --> 16:02.890
Hey, wait—

16:03.980 --> 16:05.630
No, I—

16:03.980 --> 16:07.090
Just leave it to me!

16:11.860 --> 16:13.910
I brought you some medicine and water.

16:14.200 --> 16:16.860
Th-Thank you very much...

16:21.910 --> 16:28.460
I also bought some head-cooling pads, 
masks, gelatin, and sports drinks.

16:29.280 --> 16:32.220
You're like an older sister, Koishikawa-san.

16:32.850 --> 16:35.640
Well, I do have a little brother!

16:35.640 --> 16:37.600
I'm used to taking care of others!

16:37.890 --> 16:42.650
By the way, about what you were saying 
earlier... You have an older sister?

16:45.090 --> 16:46.200
Yes...

16:46.200 --> 16:49.110
I have a sister who's a bit older than me.

16:49.780 --> 16:53.350
Though she died some years ago...

16:53.350 --> 16:54.200
Huh?

16:54.530 --> 16:59.170
I-I'm so sorry. I had no idea. 
I figured she was still...

16:59.170 --> 17:01.700
Oh, please don't worry about that.

17:02.430 --> 17:05.710
My parents weren't home very much,

17:06.030 --> 17:09.290
so my sister was like a parent to me.

17:10.160 --> 17:13.620
So that's why I was dreaming 
about the past and ended up

17:13.620 --> 17:16.110
saying something like that in my sleep...

17:17.490 --> 17:18.970
I see.

17:19.640 --> 17:24.480
I always seem to embarrass myself 
in front of you, Koishikawa-san.

17:24.990 --> 17:28.740
Really? I've never thought 
of it as embarrassing.

17:28.740 --> 17:30.440
Oh, please.

17:31.580 --> 17:33.990
Actually, right now,

17:34.400 --> 17:37.890
I feel a bit at ease right now 
because I'm with you.

17:38.450 --> 17:41.870
Now that I know heroes 
are normal people, too.

17:42.780 --> 17:44.540
Normal people?

17:45.520 --> 17:49.670
You get hurt normally, get sick normally,

17:49.670 --> 17:53.550
have a normal family, 
and attend middle school normally.

17:54.610 --> 17:58.050
Up until now, you felt kinda out of reach...

17:58.720 --> 18:01.940
But you're really just a normal girl like me.

18:02.540 --> 18:05.680
And that's why I respect you even more...

18:05.680 --> 18:07.310
and the fact that you fight.

18:08.000 --> 18:09.390
Oh, no. I...

18:10.100 --> 18:11.630
Anyway!

18:12.080 --> 18:13.820
Well, I guess I'll get going.

18:14.320 --> 18:16.290
I don't want to stay too long and bother you.

18:16.810 --> 18:18.320
Make sure you eat this, okay?

18:18.320 --> 18:19.630
O-Okay.

18:20.540 --> 18:23.760
Thank you for everything 
today, Koishikawa-san.

18:23.760 --> 18:24.660
Bye-bye.

18:26.560 --> 18:28.700
<i>Normal, huh?</i>

18:29.570 --> 18:31.430
Oh, yeah!

18:32.640 --> 18:36.300
Starting today, I'm going 
to call you "Teru-chan."

18:37.320 --> 18:39.260
And you can call me "Iko," too.

18:40.480 --> 18:41.260
See you tomorrow!

18:43.260 --> 18:45.010
Oh... Okay.

18:47.440 --> 18:48.940
See you tomorrow...

18:57.400 --> 18:58.560
I actually said it.

19:10.200 --> 19:12.790
<i>I've always wanted to be normal.</i>

19:15.800 --> 19:19.360
<i>Not because I'm a hero...</i>

19:23.120 --> 19:25.550
<i>But being able to talk in 
front of people normally...</i>

19:28.530 --> 19:31.270
<i>Being able to look people 
in the eye normally...</i>

19:33.440 --> 19:36.270
<i>Being able to be the me 
that I like normally...</i>

19:38.390 --> 19:42.280
<i>Being able to call my friends 
by their names normally...</i>

19:44.700 --> 19:46.470
<i>I'm sure this step forward</i>

19:47.100 --> 19:49.900
<i>is meaningless for a hero.</i>

19:51.230 --> 19:53.920
<i>But... even so...</i>

19:54.850 --> 19:57.090
<i>For someone normal like me...</i>

19:59.150 --> 19:59.800
G...

20:02.870 --> 20:05.650
Good morning, I-Iko-san!

20:07.940 --> 20:10.100
<i>It's a very normal yet big step forward.</i>

20:14.830 --> 20:16.970
Morning, Teru-chan!

20:30.500 --> 20:35.080
I wonder where you could be...

20:35.080 --> 20:37.810
Oh, where could you be?

20:36.300 --> 20:37.810
Hey, you!

20:38.960 --> 20:41.700
Where the hell did Stigma go?!

20:41.700 --> 20:43.260
You know, don't you?!

20:43.680 --> 20:48.260
"You"? My name is Kufufu-san.

20:48.260 --> 20:50.550
Like I care about that! Die already.

20:50.550 --> 20:52.880
I'm asking you where he went.

20:52.880 --> 20:55.270
I dunno! He went somewhere.

20:55.490 --> 20:59.770
He went somewhere?! Does that mean 
he's planning to do something?!

20:59.970 --> 21:05.030
Dunno. As you can see, 
I'm very busy fishing right now.

21:05.280 --> 21:08.710
You moron! You can't catch anything here!

21:08.710 --> 21:11.040
That's not true.

21:11.790 --> 21:12.790
See?

21:15.430 --> 21:16.780
The hell is that?!

21:16.780 --> 21:20.500
I dunno. Probably a fishie.

21:20.920 --> 21:21.860
I don't want it.

21:22.850 --> 21:24.720
Are you looking for something?

21:26.650 --> 21:27.950
Well, you see...

21:30.660 --> 21:33.520
Tzveta-chan hasn't come home yet.

21:33.880 --> 21:38.770
I'm sure she's hiding somewhere down 
there, so I'm gonna fish her up.

21:38.770 --> 21:43.030
Are you stupid? Tzveta 
disappeared forever ago!

21:47.760 --> 21:50.520
Again, I'm Kufufu-san.

21:50.520 --> 21:53.040
That hurt! I'll kill you!

21:53.270 --> 21:56.040
Then do it. Not that I'd die.

21:56.040 --> 21:58.290
Okay, fine! I will kill you!

22:04.200 --> 22:05.680
Stop that.

22:07.410 --> 22:10.160
No one wants to fight.

22:10.880 --> 22:13.250
You must love thy neighbor.

22:13.810 --> 22:16.290
Say a prayer within your hearts!

22:17.020 --> 22:19.650
Behold! Heaven!

22:24.230 --> 22:25.180
Huh?

22:25.920 --> 22:30.780
Our master has given us 
such a wonderful world!

22:30.780 --> 22:31.660
Huh?!

22:32.820 --> 22:40.080
By sharing this world with all of humanity, 
we will be able to attain true tranquility.

22:41.850 --> 22:45.210
Hey, you! Do you know where Stigma is?!

22:45.630 --> 22:47.650
Why, yes. Of course.

22:47.650 --> 22:49.840
Our master is currently preparing...

22:50.900 --> 22:55.460
Preparing to save this world.

22:58.500 --> 23:00.600
When it comes to dreaming...

23:00.600 --> 23:04.690
It's a right that everyone 
in the world has equally.

23:05.540 --> 23:08.270
But no one dreams the same dreams.

23:08.900 --> 23:13.370
If everyone was able to 
dream the same dream...

23:13.870 --> 23:17.250
That would be such a happy thing.

23:19.410 --> 23:22.210
Now, let us sow the seeds...

23:23.460 --> 23:26.040
To create a world that will bear fruit.

23:28.560 --> 23:33.640
It'll probably take a while 
longer for the night to sleep...

23:37.140 --> 23:38.470
Just wait for me.
